; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   179  \ID COV_OS_HALCOREFREEZE
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   180     \ACCEPT XX
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   181     \REASON This function is called from Os_ErrKernelPanic() right after the panic hook has returned. As the panic hook
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   182             is the last possible exit point for the tests, Os_Hal_CoreFreeze cannot be covered in tests. Because of the
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   183             simplicity of the code, the performed code inspection results in sufficient quality.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   184  
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   185  \ID COV_OS_HALCOREASSEMBLERINSTRUCTIONDATACASE
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   186     \ACCEPT XX
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   187     \REASON This case in a switch/case instruction has not been reached. However, the result of the switch/case
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   188             construct is simply to use the same assembler instruction with different intermediate data. So each
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   189             case does the same with different data. The risk of testing just some cases is considered to be low.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   190  
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   191  \ID COV_OS_HAL_MFD15
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   192     \ACCEPT XX
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   193     \REASON This inline function is used within macros in the file "Os_Hal_Entry_Lcfg.c". The file is not analyzed in our
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   194             testsuite. Nevertheless it is assured (by review of the assembler output) that the macro is used.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   195  
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   196  Justifications for core:
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   197  
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   198  \ID COV_OS_HALPLATFORMCLZAVAILABILITY
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   199     \ACCEPT TX
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   200     \REASON The condition is hardware dependent always true. The unnecessary code parts should be
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   201             removed by compiler optimization. As the tests run on each platform, the OS is to be released for, we
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   202             always just test the code for the respective platform. No risk as the remaining code shall be optimized
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Hal_Core.c	   203             away. (Other platforms may set ACCEPT XF with a similar justification)
